  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the circle $C: x^2+y^2=4$ and the parabola $P: y^2=8 x$. If the set of all values of $\\alpha$, for which three chords of the circle $C$ on three distinct lines passing through the point $(\\alpha, 0)$ are bisected by the parabola $P$ is the interval $(p, q)$, then $(2 q-p)^2$ is equal to ________",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "80",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/GEmbLsLDZ-Av-6U62mdJIQT22iboc2hQNQGl3ugyir0.original.fullsize.png\"><br />$\\begin{aligned}\n& T=S_1 \\\\\n& x_1+y_1=x_1^2+y_1^2 \\\\\n& \\alpha x_1=x_1^2+y_1^2 \\\\\n& \\alpha\\left(2 t^2\\right)=4 t^4+16 t^2 \\\\\n& \\alpha=2 t^2+8 \\\\\n& \\frac{\\alpha-8}{2}=t^2\n\\end{aligned}$<br />Also, $4 \\mathrm{t}^4+16 \\mathrm{t}^2-4 < 0$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{t}^2=-2+\\sqrt{5} \\\\\n& \\alpha=4+2 \\sqrt{5} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\alpha \\in(8,4+2 \\sqrt{5}) \\\\\n& \\therefore(2 \\mathrm{q}-\\mathrm{p})^2=80\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
